course: dictionary
lesson: 4166
title: Meet the goat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A goat is an animal with horns and often a beard, kept on farms for milk, meat and wool. Wild goats live in the mountains and are very good climbers. Read the words around goat and they often tell you which kind of goat is meant.
explain: Look at this: «At the petting farm a goat eats the corner of Maddie's map and then her coat toggle.» The word farm is a clue that this goat is a farm animal. Words like farm, mountains, milk and billy are context clues that help you understand more.
explain: Some words name a young goat, or a male or female goat. A baby goat is a kid, a male is a billy goat and a female is a nanny goat. When you see one of these words, think of the goat family.
fact: A goat is an animal with horns and often a beard.
fact: Goats are kept on farms for milk, meat and wool.
fact: Wild goats live in the mountains and are very good climbers.
fact: A baby goat is a kid, a male is a billy goat, and a female is a nanny goat.
fact: Goats are mammals and herbivores, which means they are animals that eat plants.
exercise: What is a baby goat called? | A billy goat | A flock | A nanny goat | *A kid
exercise: «Many goats have beards, both males and females; most sheep do not.» Which animal usually has a beard? | *A goat | A sheep | A horse | A cow
exercise: Wild goats live in the mountains. What are they very good at? | Swimming under water | Flying | Singing | *Climbing
test: What is a male goat called? | *A billy goat | A nanny goat | A flock | A kid
test: «The Three Billy Goats Gruff» is a story. Which animals are in the title? | *Goats | Cows | Pigs | Sheep
exam: What does «nibble a bit of everything» tell you about goats? | *Goats eat lots of different things, a little at a time | Goats only eat one kind of grass | Goats only eat meat | Goats never eat anything
